---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="PRIVACY"
  updated="Effective: 24 August 2026"
>
  <p>Vardox Studio ("we", "us") operates <strong>book.vardoxstudio.com</strong> and sells the digital edition of <em>The 65% Rule</em>. This policy explains what personal information we collect, why, and how we protect it.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>When you buy:</strong> your name, email address and mobile number, plus the PayU transaction reference. This is needed to complete and verify your payment and to deliver the digital book.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment details:</strong> card, UPI and banking details are entered only on PayU's secure checkout. We never see or store your card, UPI or banking information.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic usage data:</strong> our hosting may keep standard logs (IP address, browser type, pages visited) for security and performance.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To process and verify your purchase with PayU;</li>
    <li>To email you the digital book and your order reference;</li>
    <li>To answer support questions;</li>
    <li>To comply with legal and tax obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or share your personal information with anyone except our payment processor (PayU) where required to complete your transaction, or where the law requires it. We do not send marketing emails unless you separately opt in.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Order records (name, email, mobile, transaction reference, amount, date) are kept as long as needed for delivery, refunds, and legal/tax record-keeping.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data, subject to legal and tax retention requirements. Email <a href="mailto:shubhupublication@gmail.com">shubhupublication@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We use encrypted connections (HTTPS) across the site. Payment processing is performed by PayU under their security standards; we do not store payment credentials.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be reflected by updating the "Effective" date above.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
